1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,010
In 1869, a French sculptor painted this.

2
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:08,970
A giant woman in robes, holding a light
over the entrance to the Suez Canal.

3
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:12,370
17 years later, he unveiled this.

4
00:00:12,870 --> 00:00:16,010
So was the Statue of
Liberty built for Egypt?

5
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:19,190
People were asking that
the month she was unveiled.

6
00:00:19,370 --> 00:00:23,130
And the answer they printed
is better than yes or no.

7
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:30,850
The sculptor was Frédéric Auguste
Bartholdi, from Colmar in Alsace.

8
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:37,770
In 1855, at 21, he went up the Nile for
four months with a group of painters.

9
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:41,490
He came back obsessed
with the colossal statues.

10
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:46,550
He wrote that they seemed to be "still
listening to the most remote antiquity."

11
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:50,850
14 years later, Egypt was
about to open the Suez Canal.

12
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:55,290
Its ruler, the Khedive Isma'il,
wanted Egypt to look like

13
00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:59,290
a modern country, and Bartholdi
had an idea to sell him.

14
00:00:59,610 --> 00:01:02,910
He met the Khedive in Paris in 1867,

15
00:01:03,110 --> 00:01:07,170
and in 1869 he went out
to Egypt with his pitch.

16
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:10,590
A lighthouse in the shape of a woman.

17
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:14,210
An Egyptian peasant, a
fellah, in long robes,

18
00:01:14,230 --> 00:01:16,830
holding a lamp over the
harbour at Port Said.

19
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:20,930
He called it "Egypt
Carrying the Light to Asia."

20
00:01:21,230 --> 00:01:26,590
The figure would have been 86 feet
tall, standing on a pedestal of 48.

21
00:01:27,270 --> 00:01:29,910
He made clay models and watercolours.

22
00:01:30,330 --> 00:01:32,930
Some of them are still
in his museum in Colmar.

23
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:35,030
The answer was no.

24
00:01:35,410 --> 00:01:39,710
The canal had cost a fortune, and the
Khedive couldn't afford a colossus.

25
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:43,470
According to one account,
it was the canal's builder,

26
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:46,930
Ferdinand de Lesseps,
who told Bartholdi so.

27
00:01:47,470 --> 00:01:50,670
So Port Said got a
lighthouse, just not his.

28
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:54,570
A plain tower of concrete, 56 metres tall,

29
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:59,010
finished in time for the canal's
opening in November 1869.

30
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:00,810
It's still standing.

31
00:02:02,074 --> 00:02:04,690
Bartholdi didn't let go
of the idea of a giant.

32
00:02:05,110 --> 00:02:08,610
In France, he'd fallen in
with Édouard de Laboulaye,

33
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:11,030
a scholar who admired American democracy

34
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:14,010
and wanted France to
give America a monument.

35
00:02:14,641 --> 00:02:18,930
In 1871, Bartholdi sailed
to New York to find a site.

36
00:02:19,350 --> 00:02:21,430
Within three months he'd picked one:

37
00:02:21,610 --> 00:02:24,910
a small island in the
harbour, Bedloe's Island.

38
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:28,850
Liberty was built in Paris,
in thin hammered copper

39
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:32,650
over an iron frame
engineered by Gustave Eiffel.

40
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:37,890
From the top of her base to the
tip of the torch she's 151 feet.

41
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:41,890
She was unveiled on the
28th of October, 1886.

42
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:46,770
And that same month, the rumour
was already in the papers.

43
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:50,590
A paragraph printed across
America said Bartholdi

44
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:53,630
had first made the goddess
"to represent Commerce",

45
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:56,330
as a lighthouse for the Suez Canal,

46
00:02:56,730 --> 00:03:01,610
and that when the Khedive didn't like
it, it was "palmed off" as Liberty.

47
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:04,330
The same paragraph answered it.

48
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:07,490
Yes, Bartholdi had made
a sketch of "a figure

49
00:03:07,510 --> 00:03:10,230
of Egypt with the face
of a female fellah."

50
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:13,850
But, it said, that sketch "does not at all

51
00:03:13,870 --> 00:03:16,310
resemble the one now on Bedloe's island."

52
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:21,730
So the papers that spread the story also
printed the best evidence against it.

53
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:24,070
Put them side by side.

54
00:03:24,350 --> 00:03:29,310
A robed woman, a light held high, a
colossus at the mouth of a harbour.

55
00:03:29,810 --> 00:03:31,250
It's the same idea.

56
00:03:31,410 --> 00:03:35,790
But it's a different figure, a
different costume and a different face.

57
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:40,910
And the Egypt statue would have been
only a little over half Liberty's height.

58
00:03:41,370 --> 00:03:43,090
And the version you might have heard,

59
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:45,830
that Liberty was
"originally a Muslim woman"?

60
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:49,110
There's no trace of that in
any source from the time.

61
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:51,830
It comes from a 2015 headline.

62
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:54,630
The article underneath it says "peasant".

63
00:03:55,210 --> 00:03:58,130
So was Liberty built for Egypt? No.

64
00:03:58,250 --> 00:04:01,530
But the idea Bartholdi took
to Egypt didn't die there.

65
00:04:01,550 --> 00:04:04,270
It changed its clothes
and crossed an ocean.

66
00:04:05,130 --> 00:04:07,070
There's one more statue in this story.

67
00:04:07,090 --> 00:04:11,530
In 1899, Port Said did
get a colossal figure

68
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:15,530
at the mouth of the canal:
Ferdinand de Lesseps himself.

69
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:21,410
In 1956, during the Suez Crisis,
he was pulled off his pedestal.

70
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:24,450
The pedestal is still there, empty.

71
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:29,170
The statue survives, reportedly
in a shipyard across the water.

72
00:04:30,010 --> 00:04:33,350
So the statue they did put
up at the canal came down.

73
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:38,810
And the one they didn't is still
holding her light up, 5,600 miles away.

74
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:40,830
This was UNBUILT.

75
00:04:41,310 --> 00:04:45,670
Every picture in this video is real,
and the sources are in the description.

